    "<p>Brampton Plan-Schedule 6b-Valleyland and Watercourse Corridors <span style='background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(20,20,20); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>are interconnected natural systems associated with rivers, streams, and valley features that facilitate water movement, wildlife habitat, and ecological connectivity. These corridors perform important environmental functions while supporting recreation, active transportation, and natural heritage conservation.</span></span></p><p><span style='background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(20,20,20); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>This data is intended to be used in conjuction with other related mapping layers for this schedule, and may be impacted by other schedules, with consideration to the text of Brampton Plan.</span></span></p>"
